---
description: Always play GIFs via DOM overlays or CSS — never canvas drawImage
alwaysApply: true
---

# Animated GIFs

GIFs in this project exist for animation quality. If a `.gif` is on screen, it must play.

Canvas `drawImage()` only paints frame 1 and freezes the rest. Never draw a GIF onto canvas.

## Moving sprites

Use a real `<img>` overlay, positioned over the canvas, and remove it on hit, despawn, or reset.

Match `createBeeElement` / hearts / explosions in `public/games/dynamite/game.js` and `makeExplosionEl` / coin overlays in `public/games/snow-throw/index.html`.

```js
// BAD — frozen
ctx.drawImage(beeImg, bee.x, bee.y, size, size);

// GOOD — plays
el.src = 'images/bee.gif';
el.style.left = (canvas.offsetLeft + bee.x) + 'px';
el.style.top = (canvas.offsetTop + bee.y) + 'px';
```

## Full-bleed or static decoration

Use CSS `background-image` (Dynamite `tree.gif`, Snow Throw `lava2.gif`, site vibe backgrounds).

## Do not inspect GIF binaries

Do not `Read` GIF files in chat. Vision rejects animated GIFs and can stall the thread. Use the path/filename only.
